From: tieziyun <tieziyun@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: xlnx: add digilent,hdmi to compatible components list

The xlnx DRM master only binds components whose compatible string is in
xlnx_compatible_components_list. The out-of-tree Digilent HDMI encoder
(digilent,hdmi) registers itself as a component and is discovered
through the of_graph endpoint on the xlnx,pl-disp node, but the
whitelist filter skips it, so the master match never completes and no
DRM device is created. Add the compatible so the encoder can bind, as
it did on 5.15 kernels that predate this filter.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [enables out-of-tree driver]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_drv.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_drv.c
@@ -323,7 +323,8 @@ static const char * const xlnx_compatible_components_list[] = {
 	"xlnx,vpss-scaler",
 	"xlnx,vpss-scaler-2.2",
 	"xlnx,sdi-tx",
 	"xlnx,bridge-v-tc-6.1",
+	"digilent,hdmi",
 };

 static bool xlnx_check_compatible_component(struct device_node *node)
